Hello 3D Printing Industry team,

a news tip about a software release that addresses a specific gap in the AM
workflow.

The gap: a downloaded STL contains triangles and no construction history. CAD
systems cannot edit it meaningfully, mesh tools can edit it but never return
exact surfaces. Anyone who needs a downloaded part to fit something has to
rebuild it.

Solidon3D 0.5.0 closes part of that gap. It recognises holes, slots,
countersinks, bosses, threads and other features in an imported mesh, and as
of this release those features stay exact when they are edited: moving,
duplicating, rotating and removing them keeps real faces and edges rather than
converting to triangles. STEP import and export are part of the round trip.
The options that used to expose the underlying kernel choice have been
removed; the software keeps the exact body where it can and names the limit
where it cannot.

For readers concerned with data integrity, two details matter:

* Every dimension states its provenance in the feature window — measured,
  fitted, or taken from the construction step.
* A feature keeps its identity through edits. Closing a hole and drilling a
  new one produces the same geometry but a different feature; any fit pointing
  at it loses its reference. Moving it keeps the reference.

Also in this release: a honeycomb pattern, knurl or rib structure is
recognised as one feature with pitch, cell width and depth instead of hundreds
of faces, and can be removed or reapplied, including on a cylindrical handle;
dimensions are edited directly on the model; resin printers are supported with
pixel size and minimum wall; and a model with open areas is closed while it is
read instead of merely reported.

70 user-visible changes in this release; 896 since the first 0.1 demo.

Solidon3D is an independent development from Germany. Desktop for Windows,
macOS and Linux, one-time purchase, no subscription, fully usable offline
after a single activation, no account and no telemetry. AI features exist, are
optional, and can run locally.

